monolito-gtk-greeter for Debian and Linux Mint
==============================================

This package intentionally uses the binary package name lightdm-gtk-greeter so
that it upgrades the distribution package and owns the same greeter executable.

The configuration in /etc/lightdm/lightdm-gtk-greeter.conf is a dpkg conffile.
Local administrator changes are preserved across upgrades. Review any dpkg
prompt about that file instead of replacing it blindly.

The package does not join the host to Active Directory or configure PAM, SSSD,
winbind or Kerberos. Complete that system integration separately before testing
manual UPN or DOMAIN\\user login.
